<details><summary>Reveal the sharp bound</summary>
If $b(a)\ge\varepsilon t(a)$, then $t(a)/b(a)\le1/\varepsilon$. Therefore $\mathbb E_b[(t/b\,g)^2]\le\varepsilon^{-1}\mathbb E_t[g^2]$. For $b=(\varepsilon,1-\varepsilon)$, $t=(1,0)$, and $g=(1,0)$, equality holds.
</details>

